# CPR Look & Feel — FROZEN (Jul 27, 2026)

The CPR public site visual system is **frozen**. Do not change how the site looks or feels unless the user **explicitly** says to redesign, restyle, or unfreeze look-and-feel.

## Allowed without unfreeze

- URL / link destination fixes (e.g. Apply Now → Google Form)
- Content copy edits when asked (quotes, bullets) **without** changing layout, spacing, imagery treatment, or chrome
- Contrast-only text color fixes when explicitly requested (e.g. gray → white on testimonials)
- Auth, portal, admin, deploy, and bug fixes that preserve presentation

## Forbidden without explicit unfreeze

- Hero / gallery / image CSS (`object-fit`, `background-size`, masks, min-heights, order)
- Typography, color system, section composition, card treatment
- "Polish", "mobile fix", or photo-crop experiments that alter homepage atmosphere
- Expanding About / testimonials into new visual patterns
- Rewriting landing-chassis CSS for aesthetics

## Quarantined

Photo-crop / `object-fit: contain` homepage treatment — see `docs/_quarantine/photo-crop-contain-lookfeel/README.md`.

## If unsure

Ask: **"Does this change how CPR looks or feels?"** If yes → stop and ask the user before coding.
